messages.tutor:
Multiplying by 3 seconds adds up the displacement over that time: at \(4\,\text{m/s}\), you travel 4 metres each second.

\[
\text{Area} = 4\,\frac{\text{m}}{\text{s}}\times 3\,\text{s}
=12\,\text{m}
\]

The seconds cancel because \(\text{s}/\text{s}=1\). The area under the velocity–time graph represents **displacement: 12 metres**.
